   * by default"): the HIGH byte of each 16-bit pixel must be sent first.
   * LVGL's draw buffer is little-endian (low byte first), so every
   * 2-byte pixel must be swapped before SPI_SNDBLOCK — exactly what the
   * IDF does ("because SPI LCD is big-endian, we need to swap the RGB
   * bytes order").  The 3WIRE path already swaps; the non-3WIRE path was
   * missing it, so every pixel reached the panel byte-swapped:
   * red->blue, green->red, blue->green (confirmed by `plant img test`). */

  for (i = 0; i < count; i++)
    {
      FAR const uint8_t *src = buff + (i * (size + skip));

      for (j = 0; j + 1 < size; j += 2)
        {
          rowbuff_be[j]     = src[j + 1];
          rowbuff_be[j + 1] = src[j];
        }

      SPI_SNDBLOCK(dev->spi, rowbuff_be, size);
    }
#endif

  SPI_SELECT(dev->spi, SPIDEV_DISPLAY(0), false);
  SPI_LOCK(dev->spi, false);
}

